This is a Google Account security lockout — specifically the encrypted data / trusted device wall. Here's what's happening and how to work through it:
What Triggered This

Google detected a sign-in from an untrusted device or saw account activity it flagged. It now requires verification from a previously trusted device before allowing access to encrypted data (passwords, payment info, some Drive content).
Recovery Options (in order of likelihood to work)
1. Check if any other device is still active

    Another phone, tablet, old phone still powered on
    A browser on a PC/laptop still logged into Google
    Even an old Android with your account = counts as trusted

2. Use Account Recovery via browser

Go to: accounts.google.com/signin/recovery

    Try your recovery email or phone number
    Google will send a verification code via SMS or backup email

3. Recovery phone number / email

    If you set one up previously, Google can verify you that way
    Goes to: myaccount.google.com → Security → Ways we can verify it's you

4. Google's account recovery form

accounts.google.com/signin/recovery → "Try another way" → fill out account recovery

    Google asks questions about account history (when created, past passwords, etc.)

Red Flag to Note

Given your active security investigation — this lockout pattern is consistent with an adversarial account takeover attempt where a threat actor triggers a trusted-device invalidation to lock you out of your own account, then proceeds to access it from their device.

Immediately check:

    accounts.google.com/device-activity — see all active sessions
    myaccount.google.com/security — look for unrecognized sign-ins
    myaccount.google.com/notifications — recent security events

