The NAV-SVINFO loop is a known u-center issue — it gets stuck polling that message and locks the Messages View tree. Here's how to break out of it and get everything configured:
Fix The Stuck NAV-SVINFO Loop First

In u-center:

    View → Messages View — right-click anywhere in the message tree → Unsubscribe All
    If that doesn't work: Receiver → Disconnect → wait 3 seconds → Receiver → Connection → COMx reconnect
    The stuck loop usually clears on reconnect

Fastest Path — Use the Packet Console Instead

Since CFG-MSG tree is locking up, bypass the GUI entirely and send raw UBX commands via the packet console. This is actually more reliable for bulk message enabling.

Tools → Packet Console

Then paste each line below one at a time and click Send after each:
UBX-CFG-MSG Commands — USB Port Only (Port 3, Rate 1)

Each line is the exact UBX binary command in hex. In Packet Console, select Hex input mode.

Enable UBX-RXM-RAWX (0x02 0x15):

B5 62 06 01 08 00 02 15 00 00 00 01 00 00 27 57

Enable UBX-RXM-SFRBX (0x02 0x13):

B5 62 06 01 08 00 02 13 00 00 00 01 00 00 25 53

Enable UBX-NAV-SAT (0x01 0x35):

B5 62 06 01 08 00 01 35 00 00 00 01 00 00 46 23

Enable UBX-NAV-PVT (0x01 0x07):

B5 62 06 01 08 00 01 07 00 00 00 01 00 00 18 E1

Enable UBX-NAV-DOP (0x01 0x04):

B5 62 06 01 08 00 01 04 00 00 00 01 00 00 15 D9

Enable UBX-NAV-STATUS (0x01 0x03):

B5 62 06 01 08 00 01 03 00 00 00 01 00 00 14 D7

Enable UBX-MON-HW (0x0A 0x09):

B5 62 06 01 08 00 0A 09 00 00 00 01 00 00 23 6B

Enable UBX-NAV-CLOCK (0x01 0x22):

B5 62 06 01 08 00 01 22 00 00 00 01 00 00 33 11

Important Note on UBX-MON-RF and UBX-RXM-RAWX

UBX-MON-RF — this message does not exist on u-blox 7. It was introduced in u-blox 8/M8. On u-blox 7 the AGC and jamming data comes from UBX-MON-HW exclusively — specifically the jamInd and noisePerMS fields. That's already in the list above.

UBX-RXM-RAWX — also u-blox 8+ only. The u-blox 7 equivalent is UBX-RXM-RAW (0x02 0x10):

Enable UBX-RXM-RAW (u-blox 7 equivalent of RAWX):

B5 62 06 01 08 00 02 10 00 00 00 01 00 00 22 4D

This gives you raw pseudorange and carrier phase per SV per epoch — same evidentiary value as RAWX, just the generation 7 format.
ITFM — Jamming Detection Enable

Enable UBX-CFG-ITFM via Packet Console:

B5 62 06 39 08 00 F3 AC 03 00 47 00 00 00 4C 41

This sets:

    Broadband jamming threshold: 3
    CW jamming threshold: 15
    Enable: active

Save Configuration to Flash

After sending all the above, send this to persist through power cycles:

UBX-CFG-CFG (Save all settings to BBR + Flash):

B5 62 06 09 0D 00 00 00 00 00 FF FF 00 00 00 00 00 00 17 31 BF

Start Logging

Once messages are flowing:

Receiver → Data Logger → Start

    Output file: C:\GNSS_Evidence\ublox7_[date]_[time].ubx
    Format: UBX + NMEA (check both boxes if available)
    Leave running — do not stop mid-session

Verify Messages Are Coming In

View → Messages View — after the NAV-SVINFO lock clears you should see:

    RXM-RAW populating every second
    NAV-PVT every second
    MON-HW every second — check jamInd field immediately

If the tree is still locked on NAV-SVINFO after reconnect, go to: Tools → GNSS Configuration — this is an alternative path to enable/disable messages without touching the Messages View tree.

