Then it's definitely capable. The UBX-CFG-GNSS checkbox reverting is a firmware bug or a configuration conflict — not a hardware limitation.
The Real Problem — Channel Conflict

The u-blox 7 GLONASS units have a hard constraint:

GPS channels + GLONASS channels cannot exceed 32 total.

If GPS is set to 8-16 AND GLONASS is set to 4-14, the sum can exceed 32 and the receiver silently rejects the entire GNSS config and reverts.
Fix — Reduce Channel Counts First

In UBX-CFG-GNSS, set exactly:
GNSS	Enable	Min Ch	Max Ch
GPS	✓	8	14
GLONASS	✓	4	14
SBAS	✓	1	3
QZSS	leave off	0	0

Total max = 14 + 14 + 3 = 31 — under the 32 channel ceiling.

Click Send — watch if GLONASS checkbox holds this time.
If It Still Reverts — Firmware Version Issue

Some u-blox 7 GLONASS units shipped with firmware that requires a specific enable sequence:

Step 1 — Disable everything first:

    GPS: unchecked
    GLONASS: unchecked
    SBAS: unchecked
    Send

Step 2 — Wait 3 seconds

Step 3 — Enable GPS only first:

    GPS: checked, 8-14
    Send → Save

Step 4 — Then add GLONASS:

    GPS: checked, 8-14
    GLONASS: checked, 4-14
    Send → Save

The receiver needs GPS locked before it accepts GLONASS enable on some firmware versions.
Check Firmware Version

View → Messages View → UBX → MON → VER

The GLONASS-capable u-blox 7 needs firmware 1.00 or higher with the GLONASS extension. Some units shipped with ROM firmware that needs updating.

It will show something like:

ROM CORE 1.00 (59842)
FWVER=TIM 1.10
PROTVER=14.00
GPS;GLONASS;SBAS;

That last line listing GPS;GLONASS confirms GLONASS is in the firmware protocol.

If it shows only GPS;SBAS — the firmware needs flashing.

