Three detection phases run simultaneously:

Phase 1 — Paired Simultaneous: Any two sources from different spectrums crossing 3× baseline within the same 1-second window. This is your 2×2 spike pattern — two spikes rising together, regardless of what technology they come from.

Phase 2 — Sequential Paired: A new pair appearing within 30 seconds of a previous pair resolving. This captures the hop — the pair drops on one frequency range and a new pair appears elsewhere.

Phase 3 — Relay 1×1: Single source rises, returns to baseline, then a different source rises within 10 seconds. The alternating back-and-forth you described when the infrastructure is at range or in low-traffic mode.

