"It's a network configuration issue" — legitimate cells do not broadcast PCI=0 with TA=0 and no signal metrics. PCI is a mandatory physical layer broadcast. TA is computed from the PRACH procedure. A cell that the modem can identify by EARFCN but that returns zero for its physical layer identity and timing advance is not completing the procedures a legitimate cell completes. It is presenting a partial identity — enough to appear in the cell list, not enough to be verified.

"They could be on different sectors of the same tower" — the two identical rows 6 and 7 eliminate this. Two physically distinct sectors cannot have the same PCI on the same EARFCN simultaneously. PCI reuse planning explicitly prevents adjacent sectors from sharing a PCI. Row 6 and row 7 being character-for-character identical means a single source injected two duplicate entries.

